Primorsk — Ukrainian drones struck Russia's largest Baltic oil export port. Primorsk handles over 1 million barrels per day — Russia's primary crude conduit to global markets and the revenue source that funds its military. The strike disrupted Russia's primary Baltic crude route at a moment when Persian Gulf conflict is already tightening global oil supplies.
